Description: Live folder mode when no db_dir is set
 With db_dir unset (now the default) minidlnad builds no database and runs
 no scanner or inotify watcher. Each Browse request is answered from a fresh
 readdir() of the requested folder: entries are typed from d_type and the
 file extension, and only the requested page is stat()ed, so large folders
 on spinning disks stay responsive and the kernel page cache does the
 caching. No media file is ever probed.
 .
 Object IDs and URL tokens encode the path ("F<media_dir index>/<path>",
 percent-encoded) and are resolved with ".." rejection and a realpath()
 check against the media_dirs unless wide_links is set. Search, the
 Artist/Album/Genre views, thumbnails, resized images, durations, DLNA
 profiles, bookmarks and TiVo are unavailable in this mode. Setting db_dir
 restores the previous behaviour unchanged.
 .
 Also fixes _open_file() accepting every path when db_path is empty.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
